    "name": "translate()",
    "syntax": "transform: translate(x, y); | translateX(x); | translateY(y);",
    "desc": "Moves the painted box without touching layout. Percentages resolve against the element's own size.",
    "example": "/* centre a tooltip that was placed with left: 50% */\n.tooltip {\n  position: absolute;\n  left: 50%;\n  bottom: calc(100% + 8px);\n  transform: translate(-50%, 4px);\n}\n\n.lift {\n  transform: translateY(-6px);\n}",
    "lang": "CSS",
    "source": "content/ref/css-animation.json",
    "markdown": "`translateX(-50%)` shifts by half the element's own width, which works at any width, unlike a fixed negative margin. A single argument to `translate` sets x only; y stays at 0.\n\nTranslation is independent of `transform-origin`, unlike rotate, scale and skew.",
    "html": "<p><code>translateX(-50%)</code> shifts by half the element&#39;s own width, which works at any width, unlike a fixed negative margin. A single argument to <code>translate</code> sets x only; y stays at 0.</p>\n<p>Translation is independent of <code>transform-origin</code>, unlike rotate, scale and skew.</p>"
