    "example": "/* a chevron built from two borders */\n.chevron {\n  display: inline-block;\n  width: 8px;\n  height: 8px;\n  border-right: 2px solid currentColor;\n  border-bottom: 2px solid currentColor;\n  transform: rotate(45deg);\n  transition: transform 160ms ease;\n}\n\n[aria-expanded=\"true\"] .chevron {\n  transform: rotate(-135deg);\n}",
    "lang": "CSS",
    "source": "content/ref/css-animation.json",
    "markdown": "The origin defaults to the centre, so a square rotated by 45 degrees becomes a diamond with even gaps. `rotate(1turn)` and `rotate(360deg)` are the same angle.\n\nRotating an element that also holds a tooltip moves the tooltip with it, because the whole box is transformed.",
    "html": "<p>The origin defaults to the centre, so a square rotated by 45 degrees becomes a diamond with even gaps. <code>rotate(1turn)</code> and <code>rotate(360deg)</code> are the same angle.</p>\n<p>Rotating an element that also holds a tooltip moves the tooltip with it, because the whole box is transformed.</p>"
