    "group": "Animation",
    "name": "animation-iteration-count",
    "syntax": "animation-iteration-count: 1 | 3 | infinite;",
    "desc": "How many passes run. Fractional values are legal and stop mid pass.",
    "example": ".blink {\n  animation: blink 900ms steps(1, end) infinite;\n}\n\n.once {\n  animation: fade-in 400ms ease 1 both;\n}\n\n/* half of the second pass, then it stops */\n.halfway {\n  animation: slide 1s ease 1.5 both;\n}",
    "lang": "CSS",
    "source": "content/ref/css-animation.json",
    "markdown": "`infinite` animations never finish, so `animationend` never fires for them. Anything relying on that event must target a finite animation instead.",
    "html": "<p><code>infinite</code> animations never finish, so <code>animationend</code> never fires for them. Anything relying on that event must target a finite animation instead.</p>"
