    "syntax": "List.of(a, b, c)",
    "desc": "Builds a fixed size, immutable list in one line. Useful for seed data and test fixtures.",
    "example": "List<String> cities = List.of(\"Budapest\", \"Vienna\", \"Praha\");\n// cities.add(\"Rome\");   // UnsupportedOperationException\n\n// A mutable copy when the report needs to sort or edit it.\nList<String> editable = new ArrayList<>(cities);\neditable.add(\"Rome\");",
